; perlin noise is smooth randomness: slow shapes with finer ripples on top
; (:octaves adds ripple layers, :persistence sets how strong they are). On a
; modulator's TL it makes a pad whose colour breathes rather than wobbling
; like an LFO. A stochastic curve is baked into a macro, so the breath starts
; again at each note; a different :seed per note would vary it.
(def-fm pad init-fm :alg 4 :fb 5
  :ar1 10 :dr1 0 :tl1 32 :ml1 2
  :ar2 8  :dr2 0 :tl2 8  :ml2 1 :rr2 4
  :ar3 10 :dr3 0 :tl3 30 :ml3 3 :dt3 3
  :ar4 8  :dr4 0 :tl4 10 :ml4 1 :rr4 4 :dt4 -3)

(fm1 :tempo 80 :oct 3 :len 1 pad
  (macro :tl1 (perlin 16..44 :len 1 :octaves 4 :persistence 0.6))
  c a- f g)
